{#
    A newer release is out. Instance administrators only, with update checks
    and the banner both on; `UpdateCheckService::bannerFor()` decides.

    The release notes are GitHub's page, in a new tab: a link, not a load, so
    nothing on this page comes from a third-party host. The link is drawn only
    when the stored page is on GitHub, over https.

    Dismiss is a form. With script, htmx posts it and the banner's contents go
    but the `role="status"` region stays, emptied, so a screen reader hears
    it change, and focus moves to the page heading rather than falling to the
    top of the page (`data-focus-after`); without script, the post reloads the
    dashboard without it. Either way it stays gone for this administrator
    until a newer release appears. The form posts the version shown, so a
    release found since the page was drawn still gets its own banner.

    `banner`  the UpdateBanner
#}
<div class="alert callout update-banner" role="status" id="update-banner">
    <p class="update-banner-text">
        {{ icon('info') }}
        <span>
            {{ t('updates.banner', {'latest': banner.latestVersion, 'current': banner.currentVersion}) }}
            {% if banner.releaseUrl %}
                <a href="{{ banner.releaseUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                    {{- t('updates.release_notes') -}}
                    <span class="visually-hidden"> {{ t('updates.new_tab') }}</span></a>
            {% endif %}
        </span>
    </p>

    <form method="post" action="/updates/dismiss"
          hx-post="/updates/dismiss" hx-target="#update-banner" hx-swap="outerHTML"
          data-focus-after="#page-heading">
        {{ csrf_field() }}
        <input type="hidden" name="version" value="{{ banner.latestVersion }}">
        <button type="submit" class="button button-quiet">{{ t('updates.dismiss') }}</button>
    </form>
</div>
